<div class="page">
    <h2 style="font-size: 28px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">REDUCING SUBSTATION WIRING COSTS WITH IEC 61850</h2>
    <h1 style="font-size: 36px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 30px;">Reducing substation wiring costs with IEC 61850</h1>

    <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">
        <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span> (Ltd) is a Belgian electricity and gas distribution grid operator in the Walloon region in southern Belgium. In the city of Liège a large project started in <span data-field="date">{{ date }}</span> with the aim to revitalize the city neighborhood by creating an attractive urban centre. In the heart of the project was an exceptional architectural building that would house a shopping mall. To secure the distribution of electricity to the buildings and the 6 kV power distribution network a new switching substation was built, including ABB's <span data-field="product_name">{{ product_name }}</span> 61850 series IEDs. The decision to use IEC 61850 compliant substation automation IEDs paved the way to a simplified and cost efficient substation wiring contributing an orientation towards future technologies, interoperability
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">
        <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span> is the company name of the electricity and gas distribution grids operator owned by eight regional electricity distributors in Wallonia, i.e. Ideg, IGH, IGH, Interos, Interlux, Intermosane, and Sibelga. <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span> supplies millions customers with a total around of <span data-field="number">{{ number }}</span> TWh of electricity a year. Currently <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span> employs about <span data-field="number">{{ number }}</span> persons. The new multi-functional complex of Médacité is situated in Liège, in the city of Liège. Médacité combines commerce, leisure, culture and media, and is expected to draw up to <span data-field="number">{{ number }}</span> million visitors a year with its <span data-field="number">{{ number }}</span> m² of shopping area, cinemas and related services.
    </p>

    <div class="image-container">
        <img src="placeholder_image_2.png" alt="Médacité shopping centre interior" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <p style="font-size: 12px; margin-top: 10px;">Médacité shopping and entertainment centre at Liège, Belgium.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="diagram-container">
        <!-- Placeholder for the electrical diagram -->
        <img src="placeholder_diagram_1.png" alt="Electrical substation diagram" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;">
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 20px;">
        The secured power system of the Médacité shopping and entertainment centre at Liège, Belgium.
        The selected power system layout focuses on maximum reliability and availability of the power supply.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Power distribution in Médacité</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">
        The new <span data-field="number">{{ number }}</span> kV switching substation in the heart of Médacité is supplied by the 70/10 kV substation of Pouplin. The Pouplin substation, provided with a double busbar system, is fed from two 70/10 kV power transformers. The supply of the Médacité substation is secured by means of three parallel 10 kV cable feeders from the Pouplin substation. These cable feeders can be connected to either one of the two busbars at Pouplin. At Médacité the three feeder cables supply the dedicated sections of the switchgear. Besides the new Médacité shopping and entertainment centre and the 6 kV switching substation also an important radio station, the supply of which is secured by multiple distribution transformers. The dedicated busbar sections can be interconnected to form a ring, which enables a secured supply from another feeder cable.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">
        The Médacité substation includes ABB's air insulated switchgear well suited for applications like shopping centres and large buildings. Furthermore, the substation incorporates the novel IEC 61850 compliant Relion® 61850 series IEDs. The IEC 61850 IEDs are applied for the protection and control of the three incoming feeders and their circuit breakers and the 17 outgoing feeders. In addition, Relion® 61850 IEDs have been installed for protection and control purposes in the bus coupler bay.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="diagram-container">
        <!-- Placeholder for the communication diagram -->
        <img src="placeholder_diagram_2.png" alt="Communication network diagram" style="max-width: 90%; height: auto;">
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 20px;">
        The function of the data communication network has been secured according to the same principles as the power system network. To assure a reliable operation the networks have been designed with the same implementation principles throughout the application, from the primary circuit to the data communication solution. Ethernet switches are interconnected in a fibre optic loop to ensure redundancy. All other connections (protection IEDs, switch to RTU) are connected with a single SFTP data cable. The signals are transferred to the remote terminal unit RTU560 using the IEC 61850 protocol. The communication control centre utilizes the IEC 60870-5-104 communication protocol.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">IEC 61850, the substation automation standard of choice for ORES</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">
        <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span> has made the decision to implement IEC 61850 standard in all its large medium voltage substations. This is a result of <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span>'s orientation towards long-term stability and less dependencies of proprietary protocols. The reason for us to invest in IEC 61850 compliant technology is the ability to ensure interoperability between different vendors and implement the IEC 61850 standard. According to <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span>'s investment plan for this year we have <span data-field="number">{{ number }}</span> new substations, which are built according to the IEC 61850 standard. As we see at the moment, <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span>'s substations next year based on IEC 61850 compliant technology. <span data-field="organization.name">{{ organization.name }}</span>'s Mr Frederic de Wouters de Bouchout,
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6;">
        In Médacité the GOOSE messaging is used for earth-fault adaptation. The protection system is adapted to the varying operating states of the network. Using GOOSE messaging the protection system is informed about changes in the network operating state. For instance, when network changes are implemented using single-phase circuit breakers, the protection system is prevented by earth-fault protection system.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="image-container">
